xterm: add minimumContrast resource / -mincontrast option

Draw text whose WCAG 2 contrast ratio against its background is below
minimumContrast (default 3.0; 1 disables) lighter or darker, keeping its
hue, so application color choices such as light gray on a light
background or dark blue on black stay readable.  Applied only when
drawing, including the character under the cursor; stored colors,
screen dumps and color reports are unchanged.  Text the application
deliberately hides (same fg/bg color chosen, concealed) is left alone.
"Enable Minimum Contrast" in the VT Options menu (action
set-min-contrast) toggles it at runtime.

Also avoid X server round-trips when converting pixels on TrueColor
visuals that report more than 8 significant bits per channel, for both
the contrast filter and faint (SGR 2) colors.

Commits (branch min-contrast on xterm-412):
  3ff006f Add minimumContrast resource to keep text readable
  6029d5e Apply minimumContrast to the character under the cursor
  18f95dc Document the minimumContrast resource
  be8bc39 Add -mincontrast command-line option
  b448649 minimumContrast: avoid X server round-trips, fix cache hashing
  f3df095 Avoid X server round-trips when computing faint colors
  91c2505 Add "Enable Minimum Contrast" toggle to the VT Options menu
  5e17320 minimumContrast: only skip text whose colors were chosen equal

